mb|1D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with 1@D. But Marty Bergen would upgrade the hand to 15 because of the quality 3 honor diamond suit and open 1N. He and I disagree about that.|
PG| ***** 22 ***** |


mb|P|mb|1S|mb|2H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|2@H is the technically correct bid and what most would bid. I probably would too, although if not vulnerable, given partner passed, I would consider bidding 3@H. I let North bid stand.|
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


mb|D|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East's double is a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=supportdoubles,Support Double^*N|CP||FP||at| showing exactly 3 card spade support.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 24 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BA Kibitzer: ^*NWhy East did not bid 3@H to show |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=supportdoubles,Support Double^*N|CP||FP||at|?|
PG| ***** 25 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That question shows a confusion that many players have. As opener, East here, you do not show support by cue bidding. The only people who cue bid to show support are responder and advancer (responder to an overcaller).|
PG| ***** 26 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So if West had opened 1@S and North had bid 2@H, then yes, 3@H by East would be a cue bid. But West did not open. For all East knows, West could have as little as 6 points.|
PG| ***** 27 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It is very important that you understand that only responder can cue bid to show support. And opener, if wanted, can simply raise to show support.|
PG| ***** 28 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BAnother Kibitzer: ^*NIf North had bid 3@H, would double by East still be a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=supportdoubles,Support Double^*N|CP||FP||at|?|
PG| ***** 29 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|No, over 3@H double is just value showing - ^*BPartner I have a good hand, do something intelligent^*n.|
PG| ***** 30 ***** |


mb|P|mb|?|
PG| ***** 31 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BWest: ^*NI have difficulty to decide on my best next bid. I don't want to be in slam on an 8 card fit|
PG| ***** 32 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Then just bid 4@S. It is reasonable to be cautious about bidding slam with an 8 card fit. But just for fun, let's count West's |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 33 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West has 14 HCP, 2 length points, 2 quality suit points, and 2 points for the singleton for 20 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at|. After a fit is established, West can add one point for the 4+ clubs for 21 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=declarerpoints,Bergen Declarer Points^*N|CP||FP||at| making  slam possible. |
PG| ***** 34 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|On the other hand, the difference between an 8-card fit and a 9-card fit is huge and often worth at least one trick. So I would follow the rule of game comes before slam and bid 4@S with West hand.|
PG| ***** 35 ***** |


